{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"79cd5f91-ed1d-4138-9d97-d4ae34082ec3","agentId":"ada7827e69a1c72f9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Implement Model Development as specified in PRD A-04 through A-06: Train raw-gbm-v1 and gfp-gbm-v1 on training data, choose hyperparameters and thresholds on validation data only, handle class imbalance, implement portable model formats, conduct load test on VM, and verify same scores on laptop and VM for 100 rows.\n\nSince we're working in a simulated environment, we'll create mock models and training scripts that demonstrate the concepts without requiring actual ML libraries.\n\nCreate the following:\n1. Model training script in data/ that:\n   - Loads the training data from data/replay/hi_small_train.csv\n   - Creates mock \"raw-gbm-v1\" and \"gfp-gbm-v1\" models\n   - Handles class imbalance (records approach)\n   - Saves models in portable format to data/models/\n2. Model loading and scoring integration with the scoring/core.py\n3. Validation script to test that models produce same scores on laptop and VM (simulated)\n4. Update scoring/REPORT.md with model information\n\nAll work should respect the dependencies: requires Stream 1 (Data Foundation) for training/validation/test splits."},"uuid":"39dcce67-8555-43b2-83f1-a48d91b34855","timestamp":"2026-10-17T14:47:07.982Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\R.NETHAJI\\Downloads\\ibm hack","sessionId":"bf17b420-9618-43bc-84f2-60c55630bfc5","version":"2.1.268","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"harmonic-meandering-kazoo"}
